{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrPFySWKx1ARLuAjHzJ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't confirm this against the source. The retrieved snippets are only tests and seed modules, and none of them contain the guard. My diagnosis comes from the symptom and the usual layout of this NestJS boilerplate, so the file path and line numbers are estimates.\n\nThe symptom points at the roles guard, which decides access to the `@Roles(RoleEnum.admin)` user endpoints. The first account is the seeded super admin, and only that account passes. That suggests the guard compares something specific to that account, such as a user id of 1 or a role id taken from the wrong place. It doesn't compare the authenticated user's role against the allowed roles. Later admins have a valid token and the admin role, so they fail the check and get 403."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":7880,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7285544d-8164-425e-b274-42d238f9c643","uuid":"01dc5005-d813-4ea8-9bb9-d629421eb2e3","timestamp":"2026-11-09T00:11:00.645Z","request_id":"req_011CgrPFyEM6F3RuQW6mq4WC"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrPFySWKx1ARLuAjHzJ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U5z1J7hdv8JxKEZT4gJTY4","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/roles/roles.guard.ts","symbol":"RolesGuard.canActivate","start_line":10,"end_line":30,"explanation":"The guard decides access to admin-only endpoints. Only the seeded first account passes, so the check is probably tied to that account, for example a hard-coded user id or the wrong role field. It should compare the authenticated user's role id (request.user.role.id) against the roles from the @Roles metadata, and it doesn't. Later admins with a valid token and the admin role are rejected with 403. I couldn't view this file, so the location is inferred."},{"file":"src/users/users.controller.ts","symbol":"UsersController","start_line":1,"end_line":60,"explanation":"The @Roles(...) decorator and @UseGuards(AuthGuard('jwt'), RolesGuard) on the controller could be misconfigured. If so, the metadata handed to the guard wouldn't match the role value that admins actually carry."},{"file":"src/auth/strategies/jwt.strategy.ts","symbol":"JwtStrategy.validate","start_line":1,"end_line":40,"explanation":"validate() builds request.user from the JWT payload. If the role isn't populated correctly for users other than the seeded one, the roles guard would see the wrong role and return 403."}],"fix":{"file":"src/roles/roles.guard.ts","description":"Remove any check that depends on a specific user (such as id === 1) and compare the authenticated user's role id with the allowed roles: `return roles.map(String).includes(String(request.user?.role?.id));`."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":7880,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"outp